  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Provision of Winter NFIs(Blankets, Rubber Boots) In Al-Hasakah Governorate</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">ltpgtThe project will be implemented in Al-Hasakah Governorate, in the town of Al-Yarubiyah and all its villages, which are more than 140&#xa0;villages.ltbrgt With the aim of providing support to families in need of non-food item support for the most vulnerable groups to mitigate the effects of harsh winter conditions for the host community, displaced people and returnees, we will provide the beneficiaries with basic materials that help them enhance personal warmth (blankets, rubber boots) because the region suffers from extreme cold and extreme poverty. .ltbrgtFor this reason, the project is of great importance in contributing to achieving the goal of the non-food sector because it contributes to enhancing personal warmth and protection from weather factors and the harsh winter cold.ltbrgt6,000 beneficiaries will be targeted, meaning approximately 1,200 families.ltbrgt(Each family will receive 5 blankets + 2 rubber boots: for the father and mother)ltbrgtThe targeting criteria will be:ltbrgt- Families headed by womenltbrgt- Families who have disabilities.ltbrgt-The poorest families.ltbrgt- Displaced peopleltbrgt- ReturneesltbrgtSham ElKhair Society will implement the project in accordance with quality and quality control requirements for the entire distribution service and for non-food specifications in order to meet the required needs. The project will apply mainstreaming protection through the principles of do no harm and non-discrimination in project design, implementation and monitoring. Priority will be given to the safety and security of the distribution site, in addition to meaningful access to people with disabilities, with the possibility of the distribution team going to people who are not able to reach the distribution site.lt/pgt</narrative>
  </description>
